# Firebase client config.
#
# NOTE, so this is not mistaken for a leak later: google-services.json,
# GoogleService-Info.plist and lib/firebase_options.dart all contain an `AIza...`
# key, and all three are PUBLIC BY DESIGN. A Firebase client key is an identifier,
# not a credential -- Google ships it in every compiled app binary, where anyone can
# read it. What actually protects the data is firestore.rules plus API-key
# restrictions in the Google Cloud console. The first two are ignored here only to
# keep per-developer configs out of the repo; the fact that they are already tracked
# is not a security problem.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Real secrets, in every spelling. A bare `*.env` does NOT match `.env`, `.env.txt`
# or `.env.local` -- and a duplicated credential file with a slightly different
# extension is one `git add .` away from being published permanently.
*.env
.env
.env.*
*.env.txt
*.env.bak
serviceAccount*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
key.properties

# Dependencies. node_modules WAS committed to this repo's history once (which is
# why a history secret-scan surfaces PEM blocks from node_modules/jose's own
# documentation -- false positives, but a lot of noise). It is untracked now, yet
# was never ignored, so any `git add .` would silently re-add tens of thousands of
# files. Ignore it explicitly.
node_modules/
functions/node_modules/
